Check every config value against the range of its input

qtcCheckConfig holds thirteen values inside the range of the dialog
input that shows them, and it passes five values with no test at all.

colorSelTab takes any integer. A value below zero paints a tint through
the absolute value of the alpha. A value above one hundred saturates at
the ceiling of QColor. shadowSize takes any integer as well, and the
reader hands it straight to the shadow tiles, which grow as the square
of the value. A file that holds 3000 took the dialog from 89 MB to 229
MB and did not finish inside 130 seconds. The two gbLabel position bits
exclude each other, and a file that carries both reaches five style
sites that read them in two orders. The clamp of expanderHighlight sits
behind CONFIG_DIALOG, so only the dialog build holds that factor, while
the three sibling factors hold in both builds. readDoubleList tests no
range, so customShades and customAlphas carry a number that the dialog
cannot show. The dialog writes its own clamp over the file on the first
Apply.

Hold each value inside the range of the input that shows it. The bounds
are zero to one hundred for colorSelTab and for shadowSize. A shade
takes zero to two and an alpha takes zero to one. Keep the inside bit of
the label pair, the position that the dialog and the save path already
choose. Apply the shadow size after the check, so a value out of range
never reaches the tiles. Drop the guard around the expanderHighlight
clamp.

A file inside the range reads exactly as it read before.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 6 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

